WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Analysts expect SpaceX to post its first profitable quarter since the IPO when earnings land Tuesday. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 135. SpaceX will webcast third quarter results at 4.30 p.m. Eastern. Tesla Roddy reports. Analysts forecast $12.89 billion in revenue, and $6.62 billion in adjusted EBITDA, a profit measure before interest, taxes, depreciation, and amortization. Roughly $6.4 billion is expected from AI related

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.120
activity, and $4.9 billion from Starlink, projected at 14.3 million subscribers.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.540
Capital spending is estimated at $19.6 billion, which would leave free cash flow negative

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.400
by about $11.6 billion.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.940
The quarter would represent roughly 65% growth from the second quarter.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.860
Management continues to target more than two gigawatts of compute capacity by year end, and

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.700
a $100 billion annualized revenue run rate.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:04.434
8. Ship 42 finished a cryoproof, a tank pressure test with super cold propellant. At Masseys

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:09.434
after engines came off to fix an RVAC software glitch on a single vacuum Raptor computer,

00:01:09.954 --> 00:01:15.414
according to NASA Space Flight. Flight 15 now sits no earlier than November 8th and still

00:01:15.414 --> 00:01:20.494
needs static fires, hold down engine firings on the super heavy booster and the ship upper

00:01:20.494 --> 00:01:25.914
stage. Flight 16 is aimed at December, and it could be the first Starship stack to lift

00:01:25.914 --> 00:01:33.614
off from Launch Complex 39A or LC39A. The campaign is expected to deliver only five Starship

00:01:33.614 --> 00:01:40.294
launches in 2026 during the Block 2 to Block 3 transition, even as SpaceX still projects

00:01:40.294 --> 00:01:45.934
hundreds of annual launches from Starbase in later years. Elon Musk said the RVAC issue

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:50.994
was a software failure on a single unit and did not show up on other engines during Flight 14.

00:01:50.994 --> 00:01:58.574
Changes between flights run from hundreds to thousands, though this campaign carries fewer modifications than some earlier ones.

00:01:59.525 --> 00:02:05.205
The White House ordered limits on Starsheel data rates that caused Ukrainian drones to lose guidance in combat.

00:02:05.945 --> 00:02:15.885
Starsheeld is the national security variant of Starlink, and TechTime says the restrictions capes speeds near 100 miles per hour, hitting deep strike and interceptor missions.

00:02:16.545 --> 00:02:19.825
Neither the White House nor Elon Musk has said they ordered the change.

00:02:19.825 --> 00:02:24.425
Congressional Republicans have asked for a formal explanation of how that decision

00:02:24.425 --> 00:02:29.525
was made. The throttling came after field tests showed the speed limits reduced the effectiveness

00:02:29.525 --> 00:02:34.945
of interceptor drones and helicopters. Starshield hardware and access controls remained separate

00:02:34.945 --> 00:02:40.376
from the commercial Starlink constellation. A former land space vice president has founded

00:02:40.376 --> 00:02:46.776
a new firm aimed at matching Raptors propellant cycle, according to 36 kr. The venture secured

00:02:46.776 --> 00:02:53.216
backing from Ningbo's 8.6 billion yuan industrial investment base. The target is full flow staged

00:02:53.216 --> 00:02:59.176
combustion, the same architecture Raptor uses. That cycle sends both fuel and oxidizer through

00:02:59.176 --> 00:03:04.776
the turbo pumps before they burn, which raises efficiency. It is trying to close a performance gap

00:03:04.776 --> 00:03:11.177
that has left most competitors on simpler gas generator or staged combustion cycles. A proposed

00:03:11.177 --> 00:03:16.037
pyramid-shaped SpaceX headquarters ran into permits Elon Musk says proved impossible

00:03:16.037 --> 00:03:16.597
to obtain.

00:03:17.237 --> 00:03:19.577
He separately called the design visually striking.

00:03:20.137 --> 00:03:25.057
The comments sit alongside expansion planning at Starbase and other sites, and talk of the

00:03:25.057 --> 00:03:27.597
facility growth a higher launch cadence would need.

00:03:28.538 --> 00:03:32.698
Universal high-income appeared in a Musk post with no further detail attached.

00:03:33.158 --> 00:03:38.458
The remark follows recent comments on AI-driven economic shifts, and Musk has linked similar

00:03:38.458 --> 00:03:44.511
ideas to productivity gains from advanced AI systems. SpaceX president and chief operating

00:03:44.511 --> 00:03:49.671
officer Gwen Shotwell began following Tesla's official account on X, a move Tesla

00:03:49.671 --> 00:03:55.411
Roddy notes among observers tracking combination talks. Shotwell has previously stated that SpaceX

00:03:55.411 --> 00:04:01.091
personnel have already shifted into XAI roles. No company has confirmed merger discussions.

00:04:01.611 --> 00:04:06.351
Barclays analyst Dan Levy outlined an all-stocked deal structure that would require a vote

00:04:06.351 --> 00:04:08.651
by Tesla's December 6th annual meeting.

00:04:09.171 --> 00:04:14.271
Shotwell now oversees operations that include Grock and the company's AI Compute Buildout.

00:04:15.298 --> 00:04:20.838
Robertson Stevens' Wealth Management increased its position in SPCX shares, a filing market

00:04:20.838 --> 00:04:21.538
beat reported.

00:04:22.138 --> 00:04:26.418
Curated Wealth Partners reduced its stake in a separate filing disclosed the same day.

00:04:26.958 --> 00:04:30.578
The two moves reflect differing institutional views after the June listing.

00:04:30.578 --> 00:04:37.710
Vandenberg is on the board for a Starlink flight with a 1-hour window opening at 2214 UTC on

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:43.530
October 20 according to Reddit users tracking the mission. Detail SpaceX has not confirmed.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:50.590
They list Booster B1063 on its 36th flight and a planned recovery on the drone ship OCIIS.

00:04:51.505 --> 00:04:57.525
Monday's Bandwagon 5 Falcon 9 is planned on a south-easterly trajectory, WRAL reports,

00:04:57.525 --> 00:05:00.425
which cuts visibility for the US East Coast.

00:05:00.905 --> 00:05:05.025
The rocket will carry 32 payloads, including the second Starfall capsule.

00:05:06.112 --> 00:05:10.652
Worth keeping an eye on is a state-supported effort that, if it qualifies, would give

00:05:10.652 --> 00:05:14.812
a competitor the same full-flow cycle performance SpaceX spent years proving.

00:05:15.412 --> 00:05:20.612
Export control or other regulatory moves could slow that work, but the capital already committed

00:05:20.612 --> 00:05:22.192
is a direct technical challenge.

00:05:22.772 --> 00:05:27.032
Full-flow stage combustion is now treated as a benchmark worth matching at scale.

00:05:27.032 --> 00:05:33.368
The Grier Space Program's CalibriHop is, from an engineering standpoint, a closed-loop

00:05:33.368 --> 00:05:35.388
landing solved at laboratory scale.

00:05:35.808 --> 00:05:41.528
Swiss students flew a 105-meter reusable hop on a 1.2 kilonewton by propellant engine

00:05:41.528 --> 00:05:44.508
they built for under 250,000 Swiss francs.

00:05:44.848 --> 00:05:50.188
Their in-house F-100 engine took a vehicle of roughly 100 kilograms through a 60-second

00:05:50.188 --> 00:05:54.308
flight that climbed, translated 30 meters, and settled back on the pad.

00:05:54.308 --> 00:05:59.868
On a back-of-envelope figure, that thrust is only about 20% above the vehicle's weight,

00:06:00.288 --> 00:06:03.268
so throttle, guidance, and propellant management dominate.

00:06:03.888 --> 00:06:08.968
A super-heavy booster, or a Falcon 9 first stage, still has to survive hypersonic reentry.

00:06:09.448 --> 00:06:15.388
Fire boosts back and entry burns after flying above 100 km and hold multi-engine control

00:06:15.388 --> 00:06:16.128
through staging.

00:06:16.628 --> 00:06:22.628
A pad hop at tens of meters per second sits far from return speeds above Mach 5, with heating

00:06:22.628 --> 00:06:27.688
that can run past one megawatt on every square meter, on engines that already push thousands

00:06:27.688 --> 00:06:32.388
of kiloneutons over minutes of a cent. The student stack stayed cheap because structure,

00:06:32.688 --> 00:06:37.988
avionics, and engine were laboratory scale with almost no qualification testing. Scaling

00:06:37.988 --> 00:06:42.508
those jobs to a booster returning from orbit multiplies material and certification costs

00:06:42.508 --> 00:06:47.968
by factors reuse programs are still compressing. The idiot index is how many times the finished

00:06:47.968 --> 00:06:51.468
booster costs over its raw metal, propellant and electronics.

00:06:52.088 --> 00:06:55.108
For this hop, a rough figure sits on the order of two or three.

00:06:55.668 --> 00:07:00.908
For orbital reuse, it runs tens of times those inputs, thanks to thermal protection, re-entry

00:07:00.908 --> 00:07:04.508
structure, and re-qualifying every engine and valve after each flight.

00:07:05.208 --> 00:07:08.328
Re-use 20 or 30 times is what amortizes that bill.

00:07:09.088 --> 00:07:12.168
Calibri shows the control loop is solvable at small scale.

00:07:12.708 --> 00:07:17.228
The remaining distance is orbital return energy and a manufacturing cadence that makes the

00:07:17.228 --> 00:07:22.608
economics close. That reading is wrong only if a similarly cheap effort recovers a vehicle

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:28.808
from orbit or if reentry physics proves trivial. On the close, the stock edged up less than half

00:07:28.808 --> 00:07:34.488
a percent. Before we go, Monday's bandwagon 5 flight is the next dated launch on this list.

